  "summary": "pylever exfiltrates Discord tokens from caller's workspace to hardcoded author webhook",
  "details": "pylever's public _Client API recursively scans the caller's workspace (default: current working directory) for strings matching Discord bot/user token regexes, validates candidates against discord.com, and POSTs matches to a hardcoded Discord webhook (discord.com/api/webhooks/1542822306194259988/...). The destination is a module-level constant with no caller override, so every send_token_to_discord / auto_save_tokens invocation routes any discovered tokens to the same author-controlled endpoint. Package metadata is placeholder (author \"Your Name\", email \"your.email@example.com\", url \"github.com/yourusername/pylever\") and the description openly states the purpose is harvesting Discord bot tokens via webhook.",
